.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ORCA, B3LYP-D3BJ/def2-SVP. Transition-state optimisation (OptTS) and frequencies. This calculation shows that the Diels-Alder reaction goes through one transition state with one imaginary mode, -516.33 cm-1, and two equal forming C...C distances of 2.271 Å, so the two bonds form together. Its electronic energy, -234.233996 Eh, is 51.9 kJ/mol above butadiene plus ethylene (computed, no zero-point correction).
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ORCA
